# Project roadmap

`docs/roadmap.md` is the single source of truth for what is already built vs.
what remains. Priorities currently run P0–P4+ (MVP P0–P3 first slices are
done and merged to `master`).

- Before proposing a plan for "what to build next" or "finish the project",
  read `docs/roadmap.md` first. Don't re-propose items already marked ✅ done.
- **Post-MVP:** do not block new product features on leftover polish (deploy
  docs, Sentry, deferred Playwright / Prisma integration tests) unless the
  user explicitly asks to ship or harden first.
- Default recommended next product work is **P4 — Learning plan / study focus
  from weak skills** when the user asks "what's next" without a specific
  feature. If they name a different feature, plan that slice and add it to
  the roadmap in the same change.
- Prefer one focused, shippable slice per plan. When inventing features,
  ground them in `docs/vision.md` success metrics.
- When a roadmap item is completed, update its status in `docs/roadmap.md` in
  the same change — the roadmap must stay accurate, not aspirational.
- If you discover a gap not listed in the roadmap, add it before starting
  unrelated work, so the backlog stays a reliable audit of reality.
- New work branches from current `master` (stacked chore/P0–P3 feature
  branches were merged and deleted).
